{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And Aaron and his sons shall come.</b> The order of covering the vessels of the Tabernacle: over the Ark they covered the veil, and over it a covering of תחש skin, and above they spread over it a cloth of תכלת. The table they cover with a cloth of תכלת, and upon it the utensils, and over them they cover with a cloth of תולעת שני, and over the cloth of תולעת שני they cover it with תחש skin. The menorah they cover first with a cloth of תכלת, and over the תכלת, תחש skin. The golden altar, which is dedicated for the incense, they spread over it a cloth of תכלת, and over the cloth, תחש skin. The bronze altar, which is the altar of burnt offering, they spread over it a cloth of ארגמן, which is redder than the cloth of שני, because there the sacrifices are dashed, and over the ארגמן, תחש skin. You thus learn that for all the vessels, whether they have תכלת or שני or ארגמן, all of them are covered with תחש skin, and it is the uppermost covering seen over them all, except for the Ark, which Scripture did not want to set with a covering of תחש skin like the rest of the vessels, but rather that its uppermost covering be תכלת like the essence of the heavens for purity."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:29:51.284895874Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}